  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-09-22T07:46:59.291Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Good evening. It has come to my attention that a great magnitude of VRChatters choose not to speak, and thus getting their friends attention to the fact that they created a portal can be a mundane task, especially considering that others may already be engaged in conversation, thus making it difficult to interrupt. It would seem a one-off sound effect would be both a simple and effective means to allow those nearby to be made aware of the creation of a portal. In addition, if someone is on your friend list and creates a portal in the room you are both residing, it would seem prudent to make said sound be global range for those friends. This would alleviate people running around yelling to announce the placement of a fresh portal, while also putting the portal creators mind at ease knowing that their friends are aware a portal perhaps worth visiting is available. Thank you for your time in considering this matter, and I hope we may see this solution or better soon.",
